course: dictionary
lesson: 9001
title: Compound words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sketchbook is a compound word: it joins two smaller words, sketch and book. When you meet a long word, look for small words inside it, then ask what the parts mean together. A sketch is a quick drawing, and a book has pages, so a sketchbook is a book of quick drawings.
explain: Check your idea in the sentence. «Most people will not notice one wobbly line, and you can draw over it; sketchbooks are full of wobbly lines.» If a sketchbook holds quick drawings, then full of wobbly lines makes sense, because quick drawings are not always neat.
explain: Compound words are common in English, such as playground, bedroom and toothbrush. Phrases show how a word is used. «Keep a sketchbook» tells you it is something you keep and carry, and «sketchbook page» tells you it has pages you can turn.
fact: A compound word joins two words to make a new word, like sketch and book make sketchbook.
fact: «Sketchbook» means a book of plain, often thick, paper for drawing sketches and quick pictures.
fact: A sketchbook can also be a collection of a person's sketches or quick notes.
fact: Artists often carry sketchbooks so they can draw outside.
fact: In art lessons, pupils keep a sketchbook to practise drawing, collect ideas and test colours.
exercise: «Sketchbooks are full of wobbly lines.» What is a sketchbook? | A story book about a wobbly dog | A large sheet of paper for printing posters | *A book of plain paper for quick drawings | A tin for storing paints
exercise: Which two smaller words make up sketchbook? | Sketchy and bookshop | Skate and look | *Sketch and book | Stretch and book
exercise: Ravi carries his sketchbook to the park to draw the trees. Why does he take it there? | To go to sleep | To cook his lunch | To read a long story | *To draw outside
test: «Her sketchbook page was covered in quick drawings of cats.» What is on the page? | *Quick drawings of cats | Sums for maths homework | A recipe for cake | Printed photos of the sea
test: Miss Hale looks at her pupils' sketchbooks to see their progress. What is a sketchbook used for in art lessons? | To send letters to friends | To store cereal | To wrap presents | *To practise drawing and test colours
exam: Which statement about sketchbooks is true? | *They are books of plain paper used for drawing and quick notes | They are a type of kitchen tool for baking | They are only used for printing photographs | They must never contain any wobbly lines
